## 1. Sound local-rank relaxation

Let `P` be the five-dimensional external coefficient code. The committed
nine-no-root reduction gives

`(d1,d2,d3,d4,d5)(P) >= (2,4,5,7,8)`.

For a touched block `b`, let `I_b` be the set of the nine no-root
occurrences whose tetrahedral support contains `b`.

The verifier uses the repaired one-sided local-rank rule already audited for the
selected-pair profile:

- a repeated containing tetrahedral support forces local empty-block rank two,
  so `d2>=4` forces `|I_b|>=4`;
- with no repeated containing support, `|I_b|<2` cannot be empty by
  `d1>=2`;
- with no repeated containing support and `|I_b|=2` or `3`, only local
  rank one is allowed;
- with no repeated containing support and `|I_b|>=4`, both local ranks one
  and two are allowed.

Thus every actual empty block receives at least one searched rank option.

For two searched local spaces with occurrence sets `I,J`, the pairwise
filters are only the necessary generalized-weight consequences:

- line-line: `|I intersect J|>=2` or `|I union J|>=4`;
- plane-line: `|I intersect J|>=2` or `|I union J|>=5`;
- plane-plane: `|I intersect J|>=4`, or
  `|I intersect J|>=2 and |I union J|>=5`, or `|I union J|>=7`.

A selected singleton contributes either the zero external constraint or one
rank-one constraint line. If that line is nonzero, `d1(P)>=2` forces its true
support to have size at least two. The verifier permits such a line at any
remaining touched block with at least two incidences and uses `I_b`, which is
a superset of its true coordinate support. It also permits the zero-line case.
These choices enlarge the state space.

The actual-empty spaces together with the two selected-singleton constraints
must generate the five-dimensional code `P`. The support verifier imposes
only the necessary relaxed conditions

- nominal generator dimension at least five; and
- union of their occurrence supports of size at least eight,

the latter following from `d5(P)>=8`.

## 2. Structural conditions and the touched-block bound

Let `T` be the touched block set, `h=|T|`, `C` the touched actual-complete
blocks, `e` the number of touched actual-empty blocks, and `t` the number of
the two selected singletons that lie in `T`.

Because `d_root=0`, the triangle rows of `C` are independent. The four
external relation directions also give

`rank H(T) - rank H(C) >= 4`.

Since `rank H(T)<=15`, every actual state has `|C|<=11`. As

`|C| = h-e-t`,

we obtain

`e >= h-11-t`.

The nine no-root cycles contribute exactly 36 cycle/block incidences. Every
touched block contributes at least one incidence, while every actual-empty block
contributes at least two. Therefore

`36 >= h+e >= 2h-11-t >= 2h-13`,

so every actual state satisfies

`h<=24`.

For each relaxed empty family the verifier permits `t=0,1,2`, including the
possibility that one or both selected singleton blocks are outside `T`. For
each touched singleton placement it puts the empty and selected-singleton blocks
into the virtual incomplete set `I`, and keeps a state only if

`H(T minus I)`

is independent and

`rank H(T)-rank H(T minus I) >= 4`.

For the placement corresponding to any actual state, `T minus I=C`, so both
tests are necessary. The search also admits many placements and rank labels that
need not come from a legal root state; this only makes the search a superset.

## 3. Exact support enumeration

A no-root four-cycle has one of 35 tetrahedral supports on seven labels, and a
fixed support occurs with multiplicity at most three. The imported verifier
independently checks the Burnside orbit counts

`1, 1, 4, 14, 61, 268, 1283, 6032, 27763, 121458`

for multiset sizes zero through nine and reconstructs the size-nine orbits by
canonical augmentation.

The exact executed census for the two-singleton relaxation is:

- size-nine support orbits: `121458`;
- support orbits with `|T|<=24`: `103247`;
- raw legal size-nine extensions: `966977`;
- raw legal extensions with `|T|<=24`: `802570`;
- relaxed final empty-family states: `43041`;
- singleton placements tested: `7566114`;
- surviving support orbits: `13`.

The exact surviving canonical support multisets are:

1. `[0123]^3 [0124]^3 [0134] [0234] [1234]`
2. `[0123]^3 [0124]^3 [0134] [0234] [1235]`
3. `[0123]^3 [0124]^2 [0134]^2 [0234]^2`
4. `[0123]^3 [0124]^2 [0134]^2 [0234] [1234]`
5. `[0123]^3 [0124] [0125] [0134] [0145] [0234] [1234]`
6. `[0123]^3 [0124] [0134] [0145]^2 [0234] [1234]`
7. `[0123]^3 [0124] [0134] [0145] [0156] [0234] [1234]`
