The verifier fail-closes on every census number above and on the complete
ordered list of thirteen survivors.

## 4. Exactness of triangle-row ranks

The imported triangle-row rank routine works modulo `2^31-1`, verifies that
modulus by the Lucas-Lehmer test, and uses the same Hadamard bound as the
selected-pair support certificate. Relevant triangle-row minors have squared
absolute determinant at most `3^15`, while `(2^31-1)^2>3^15`. A nonzero
integer minor therefore cannot vanish modulo the prime, so these modular ranks
equal the rational ranks.

## 5. Consequence

Every realizable two-selected-singleton state lies among the thirteen support
orbits above.

Authoritative main already has exact orientation exclusions for the first two
listed supports:

- `[0123]^3 [0124]^3 [0134] [0234] [1234]`;
- `[0123]^3 [0124]^3 [0134] [0234] [1235]`.

Consequently the unresolved orientation frontier for this profile is now
exactly the remaining eleven explicit support orbits 3 through 13 above.

This does not close the two-singleton profile, the full `D=-1,p=2` branch, or
Erdos Problem #99.
